6. Smoothing / differentiation under the integral: `t ↦ P_t f` differentiable for t > 0 with derivative `∫ (∂_t K) f` — differentiation under the integral via `hasDerivAt_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_deriv_le` (mathlib `intervalIntegral` has this for intervals; there's also `hasFDerivAt_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_lip'` for arbitrary measures in `Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Bochner`). With the heat kernel, for t in a compact interval [ε, T], the time derivative ∂_t K n t x = K · (n/(2t) ... ) is dominated. That's feasible but maybe heavy. Alternative smoothing: `x ↦ P_t f x` is differentiable/continuous for t > 0 and bounded f (differentiation under integral in space variable, dominated by polynomial × Gaussian). That could use `hasFDerivAt_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_lip'`.

